.TH BUPT 1 "2026-11-18" "bupt" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bupt \- manage BUPT model APIs, compute resources, and school sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bupt
[
.I global-options
]
.I command
[
.I arguments
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
bupt is a Unix-style client and controller for BUPT compute.
The controller runs locally by default. An optional remote controller can
continue lifecycle management while the workstation is asleep.
Previously prepared SSH routes do not require a fresh school login.
.SH GETTING STARTED
.nf
bupt init
bupt
bupt login
bupt status
bupt api model
bupt api usage
bupt api key
bupt compute catalog
bupt compute instance
bupt up experiment --preset gpu-small --max-runtime 2h
bupt ssh experiment
bupt down experiment
.fi
.PP
Configure the preset from the actual platform catalogue before allocation.
Outside the school network, a reachable direct SSH route or a configured
SSH relay is required. Automatic peer-to-peer NAT traversal is not provided.
.SH DISCOVERY
With no arguments, bupt prints the command summary and exits.
Run bupt tui to open the interactive platform overview.
Use arrows, Enter and Escape to browse, / to filter, r to refresh, and q to quit.
bupt tui api and bupt tui compute open the service directly.
The resources, work, files and access shortcuts also remain available.
Use --cached with tui to browse controller records and saved catalogues.
.PP
bupt help TOPIC shows related commands. COMMAND --help shows common flags.
bupt help COMMAND --all displays full options, and bupt help --all lists the command tree.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init, agent
Initialize, install, inspect, or run a local or optional remote controller.
.TP
.B api
Show the model service overview. Use api model for model IDs, capabilities,
context, prices and observed health. Use api usage for period totals and balance.
Use api key to list, create, enable, disable, export or delete a scoped key.
Only an explicit export releases the secret held by the selected controller.
Use api guide for the current gateway address and SDK examples.
.TP
.B compute
Show the compute workspace. Browse catalog, instance, quota, project, storage,
school scheduler jobs, managed runs, or operation receipts. Use compute features
to inspect published module settings. Administrative views verify school roles.
.TP
.B account, news, agreement
Inspect the signed-in portal account, read campus notices or review the service agreement.
.TP
.B login, logout, auth
Manage WebVPN QR approval, university SSO, and the platform callback.
University SSO uses QR by default. Use bupt login --sso-password for campus
username and password. The legacy --local option selects a compute-platform password.
The access subcommand stores the separate instance-console bootstrap password.
Use bupt logout (also available as bupt auth logout) to end the selected session
and clear saved platform and instance-console passwords. Active managed runs block
logout by default. Use bupt logout --dry-run to preview the operation.
.TP
.B profile, config
Select account profiles and inspect or change layered non-secret settings.
.TP
.B status
Show live authentication and resource status; --cached reads only saved state.
Status never starts a login or takes over another school session.
.TP
.B preset
Save verified resource choices, select defaults, or remove local presets.
The set, ls, show, use, and rm subcommands support reusable finite limits.
.TP
.B wait
Resume waiting for a durable run ID; --for finished waits for cleanup.
Interrupting a wait does not cancel the controller-owned run.
.TP
.B resources, spec, quota, estimate
Inspect personal resource limits and visible templates grouped by pool.
Use resources --cached for the saved catalogue, or spec show to inspect one template.
.TP
.B instance, up, down
Create, adopt, start, stop, release, restore, and explicitly delete instances.
.TP
.B lease
Inspect or change the current finite runtime and renewal policy.
.TP
.B run, job
Launch bounded detached jobs; inspect, follow logs, wait, cancel,
or update policy.
.TP
.B ssh, exec, proxy, forward, cp, sftp
Use cached SSH routes for terminals, commands, byte streams, port forwarding,
and file transfers.
.TP
.B console
Use the platform terminal. This path still requires platform authentication.
.TP
.B data
List, upload, or download persistent platform storage.
.TP
.B resize, snapshot, clone, service
Use capabilities actually supported by the selected platform template.
.TP
.B key, client, ssh-config
Manage dedicated instance keys, scoped controller clients,
and optional OpenSSH configuration.
ssh-config install INSTANCE --alias bupt-gpu installs a short SSH alias
with a verified host key and a recoverable configuration backup.
.TP
.B task, audit, doctor
Inspect operation receipts, sanitized controller events,
and independent health checks.
.TP
.B completion
Generate Bash, Zsh, or Fish completion scripts.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --profile " NAME"
Select an account profile.
.TP
.BR --config " FILE"
Select the trusted global TOML configuration.
.TP
.BR --project-config " FILE", " --no-project"
Select or ignore a project configuration.
.TP
.BR --controller " local|ssh://HOST", " --socket " PATH
Override the controller connection for this invocation.
.TP
.BR --json ", " --jsonl ", " --quiet
Write one JSON value, one record per line, or identifiers only.
These options are mutually exclusive and are rejected for raw SSH/proxy output.
.TP
.B --non-interactive
Do not prompt. Authentication requiring human approval returns a real error.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Validate and describe changes without applying them.
Some validation may read platform state.
.TP
.BR --timeout " DURATION"
Limit RPC waiting. Interactive SSH sessions have no default session timeout.
.TP
.BR --idempotency-key " KEY"
Reuse a stable request identifier for retries of the same intended operation.
Changing the payload with the same key is an error.
.SH RUNTIME POLICY
Managed allocation and jobs require an explicit finite
.B --max-runtime
or
.B --until
value, either from configuration or command flags.
Elapsed setup and queue time count toward the run limit.
Updating a limit does not reset the original start time.
.PP
The default cleanup policy is release: stop the instance and release its
allocation into the platform recycle bin. Delete is separate and permanent.
School authentication is still required for platform renewal and cleanup.
A sleeping local controller cannot submit these requests until it resumes.
.SH INPUT AND OUTPUT
Results and remote program bytes use stdout. Prompts and diagnostics use stderr.
Interactive terminals wait for school approval. With --sso-password, WebVPN
still uses QR. The CLI prompts for the campus username and a hidden password
only when CAS needs them. Use --username to prefill the campus ID. The
controller saves the verified session and uses the campus password once.
Without a terminal, use --device --wait and optionally --qr-file FILE.
QR filenames receive private per-stage suffixes
and never replace existing files.
For scripted campus login, combine --sso-password with --username and
--password-stdin, or with --credentials-stdin JSON containing username,
password and optional captcha_code. Use auth poll --wait to resume a staged login. Password and token argument flags are not provided.
Use -- before the remote argv of exec or run;
shell syntax is not expanded locally.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success. 1 indicates an operational failure. 2 indicates invalid
CLI usage. 130 indicates interruption. Native exec and completed jobs preserve
the remote command's exit status, so those statuses can overlap local codes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bupt/config.toml
Trusted profiles and non-secret defaults; default base is ~/.config.
.TP
.I .bupt.toml
Project selection, presets, and runtime policy. Trusted endpoint and identity
settings are not accepted from this file.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/bupt/
Controller state database and local socket; default base is ~/.local/state.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/bupt/
Encrypted credentials, protected master key, and dedicated key files;
default base is ~/.local/share.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bupt run --preset gpu-small --max-runtime 4h -- python3 train.py
bupt job run --instance experiment --max-runtime 1h --detach -- make test
bupt ssh experiment --session work --reconnect
bupt exec experiment -- printf '%s\\n' 'an exact argument'
bupt lease set experiment --max-runtime 6h
bupt lease set experiment --no-renew
bupt data pull output/model.bin - > model.bin
bupt cp --recursive ./src experiment:work/src
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.B bupt help
and
.B bupt COMMAND --help
provide the current command and option reference.
README.md documents setup and lifecycle workflows; docs/protocol.md documents
adapter evidence, transport contracts, and current limitations.
